// complete we immediately close with ">>"; otherwise we look at the number of
// valid next tokens. When the grammar is narrow, we use a hard constrained step;
// when it is broader, we bias toward the parser's top valid candidates by
// boosting their logits and sampling once. Valid sampled tokens are appended;
// invalid samples are rejected for that outer step.
// This tracked state supports valid SQL generation because currentConstrainedOut
// is always exactly the generated suffix inside the active span, so parser
// queries are made on the true SQL prefix; opening resets it to [], appending
// extends both generated and the tracked SQL prefix together, and closing is
